diff --git a/docs/preconf.md b/docs/preconf.md
index 022426a..6986c72 100644
--- a/docs/preconf.md
+++ b/docs/preconf.md
@@ -237,3 +237,18 @@ Bytes are serialized as base 85 strings. Sets are serialized as lists, and deser
 Tuples are serialized as lists, and deserialized back into tuples.
 _tomlkit_ only supports mappings with string keys so mappings will have their keys stringified before serialization, and destringified during deserialization.
 [`date`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/datetime.html#datetime.date) and [`datetime`](https://docs.python.org/3/library/datetime.html#datetime.datetime) objects are passed through to be unstructured by _tomlkit_ itself.
+
+## Decimal values
+
+The JSON, ujson, orjson, PyYAML and msgspec JSON converters support
+`decimal.Decimal`. They encode Decimal values as strings to preserve precision,
+trailing zeros, signed zero and exponents. The msgspec converter leaves encoding
+to msgspec's native implementation rather than installing a custom unstructure
+hook, preserving its optimized paths for supported classes and collections.
+
+String round-trips are exact. A number already parsed as a float may have lost
+precision, which converting it to a Decimal cannot recover. For numeric input
+handled by the Decimal structure hook, PyYAML uses `Decimal(str(value))`; the JSON converters use `Decimal(value)`.
+Native msgspec Struct handling remains delegated to msgspec and may use different
+numeric conversion rules. Use strings when exact decimal representation matters. A plain `cattrs.Converter`
+is unchanged and still needs explicit Decimal structure hooks.
diff --git a/src/cattrs/preconf/json.py b/src/cattrs/preconf/json.py
